       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. At that dose the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and prolonged toxicity, because amlodipine's half-life is 30 to 50 hours. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nThis may be a typo. Here are some options:\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the usual maximum.\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the standard starting dose, or 2.5 mg if you want a conservative start.\n- **30 mg total daily dose** intended as something else, such as adding a second agent. I can enter a different regimen if you tell me which one.\n\nIf you really do want 30 mg daily, please confirm that. I can enter it with a note that it's an intentional above-maximum dose, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it. Which would you like?"
      }
